1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,000
[roars]

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,000
[narrator] Strange beasts
and monsters...

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,000
vast riches, hidden treasures...

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,000
evil haunts, uncharted frontiers...

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
the mysterious unknown.

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,000
The people who are captivated
by the magic in those words...

7
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
are called...

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Hunters.

9
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,000
[theme song plays]

10
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:55,000
So...

11
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:58,000
I'll make sure all three of you
get safely dropped off

12
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:02,000
at the port closest to the exam site.
How does that sound?

13
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:05,000
All right!

14
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:13,000
TEST x OF x TESTS

15
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:17,000
DOLLE HARBOR

16
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:19,000
[narrator]
After winning over the old captain,

17
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Gon, Kurapika and Leorio
arrived at Dolle Harbor,

18
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,000
where their adventures
were just beginning.

19
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:29,000
Thanks a lot, Captain.
That was really fun.

20
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:33,000
[laughs] I've got to admit,
I had a pretty good time, myself.

21
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:38,000
Oh, yeah, let me give you a bit of advice
as a small token of my appreciation.

22
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:39,000
Advice, sir?

23
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Look. Do you see that big cedar tree?
The one up on the top of that hill?

24
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:46,000
[Gon] Uh-huh.

25
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,000
[Captain]
You'll wanna make your way there first.

26
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:51,000
It's a shortcut to the exam site.

27
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:54,000
[Gon] A shortcut? Great!
So, just head for that tree, huh?

28
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:58,000
Thanks for the tip, Captain.
You're the best.

29
00:02:58,000 --> 00:02:59,000
Good luck to you.

30
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:03,000
Thanks! Have a safe trip!
Take care of yourself!

31
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:10,000
[Captain] You can rest easy, Ging.
Your boy's grown into a fine young man.

32
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:14,000
[snickers]

33
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:19,000
-[Leorio] Hmm, that's odd.
-[Gon] What is?

34
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:22,000
[Leorio] Well, uh, according
to this notice I received,

35
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:26,000
the exam is supposed to be held
somewhere in Zaban City, you see?

36
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:32,000
Now, we're here, and that tree is there,
which is the opposite direction of Zaban.

37
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,000
Could you have misheard the captain?

38
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:38,000
I don't think so. He told me I should go
towards that cedar tree.

39
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,000
I see.

40
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:43,000
And this stupid notice isn't any help
at all.

41
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:47,000
It says the exam's in Zaban City,
but it doesn't say where, exactly!

42
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:51,000
Our task is to find the site
using only limited information.

43
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:55,000
This is another test to determine
if we're worthy of the Exam.

44
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:58,000
Yeah, I already knew that,
smarty pants! So give it a rest!

45
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,000
[Gon] I think I’ll check it out for myself

46
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:03,000
Find out what the captain
was talking about.

47
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:05,000
[Leorio] Whoa, whoa. Are you serious?

48
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:08,000
The bus to Zaban is gonna leave
any second!

49
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:10,000
We need to be on it when it does.

50
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:12,000
Hey!

51
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:15,000
Geez. The kid’s too trusting
for his own good.

52
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:18,000
You can’t just trust everyone
all the time.

53
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:21,000
Kurapika, come back!

54
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:25,000
I’m intrigued by the captain’s advice,
but even more so by Gon’s behavior.

55
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:28,000
I’m curious to see what he’ll do.

56
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:33,000
All right, whatever. See ya!
It wasn’t long but it was nice knowing ya.

57
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:37,000
Another follower,
just like the rest of ‘em.

58
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,000
Not me, though. I’m gonna take the bus.

59
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:41,000
[man 1] So, it was a trap?

60
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:46,000
[man 2] All I’m sayin’ is none
of the buses made it to Zaban City.

61
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:49,000
[man 1 chuckles]
Rookies always fail this part.

62
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:51,000
They believe whatever you tell ‘em!
[chuckles]

63
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:54,000
[Leorio] Hey, hey, hey, wait for me!

64
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:01,000
[Leorio] It’s just I knew you guys
would be lonely without me.

65
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:04,000
Plus, it’s no fun traveling alone!

66
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:10,000
That’s why I figured I’d stick with you
two a little while longer. [laughs]

67
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:13,000
[wind whistling]

68
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:17,000
[squawks]

69
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:21,000
[Leorio] Man, this is one creepy place.
There isn’t a single soul anywhere.

70
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:24,000
No. There’s a bunch of people here!

71
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:26,000
[gasps] What?

72
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:30,000
[all gasp]

73
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:42,000
[Leorio] What’s up with these guys?

74
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:45,000
Exciting.

75
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:47,000
"Exciting"?

76
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:49,000
Exciting.

77
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:51,000
"Exciting"?

78
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:56,000
Time for the exciting
multiple-choice quiz!

79
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:03,000
[band playing instruments]

80
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:04,000
[crow caws]

81
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:09,000
Let me take a guess. You boys are headed
for the cedar on the hill, aren’t you?

82
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:11,000
There’s only one way to get there.

83
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:14,000
You’ll have to pass
through this town first.

84
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:15,000
[all] Huh?

85
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:19,000
[old lady] You must pass a quiz
comprised of a single question.

86
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:22,000
Wait a second! What is going on here?

87
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:24,000
[old lady]
You’ll have five seconds to answer.

88
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:27,000
If you’re correct, then you can move on.

89
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:30,000
If not, you’re disqualified
from this year’s Exam.

90
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:32,000
Oh, I see.

91
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:35,000
It’s another trial we have to pass
before taking the Exam.

92
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:38,000
So that’s it, huh?
Lucky I’m an expert in quizzes.

93
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:40,000
Wait, one question?

94
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:43,000
Your answer must be
either the number one or two.

95
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:47,000
Any answer that is not the number one
or number two will be deemed incorrect.

96
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:51,000
Hold on! All three of us
have to share the same question?

97
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:55,000
So if Kurapika here gets it wrong,
it means I get disqualified, too?

98
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:58,000
Not very likely.
Although, if the roles were reversed,

99
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:01,000
-it would be all but inevitable.
-You wanna repeat that?

100
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:04,000
It's okay! Even if only one of us
knows the answer,

101
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:08,000
all three of us get to move on. [chuckles]
And I'm real bad at quizzes.

102
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:10,000
-True.
-Fair point.

103
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:11,000
[man] Hey, hey.

104
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:16,000
Hurry it up, or I might answer it
before the rest of you get a chance.

105
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:18,000
-[Leorio] So, who the heck are you?
-[Gon] You don’t know?

106
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:22,000
He’s been following us pretty closely
ever since we left the port.

107
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:23,000
[Leorio] Really?

108
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:24,000
Yeah, sorry, kid.

109
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:28,000
Didn’t mean to eavesdrop, but I couldn’t
help but hear you guys talking.

110
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:30,000
[old lady] What will you do?

111
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:33,000
[Leorio] He seems pretty eager to me.
Should we let him go first, guys?

112
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:35,000
See what kind of question
we can expect from them?

113
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:38,000
-[Gon] Sure. I'm okay with that.
-[Kurapika] No objections here.

114
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:40,000
[Matthew] Let's get to it, then.

115
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:44,000
Once I ace this quiz,
I’m gonna leave a trail of traps

116
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:46,000
for anyone who tries to follow me.

117
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:47,000
Now, here is your question.

118
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:49,000
-[horn tooting]
-[crow caws]

119
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:54,000
A group of evil villains have kidnapped
your mother and your true love

120
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:56,000
and you can only save one of them.

121
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:59,000
Choose one for your mother
or two for your true love.

122
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:02,000
Which do you save and which of them dies?

123
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:05,000
-[Gon, Leorio and Kurapika gasp]
-Hey! What kind of quiz is this?

124
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,000
[snickers]

125
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:08,000
[bell rings]

126
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:10,000
The answer’s number one.

127
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:13,000
Oh? And what's your reason?

128
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:16,000
It’s your mom!
It’s not like you can replace your mom.

129
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:19,000
But a lover,
you can always find another one.

130
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:22,000
-What?
-[crow caws]

131
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:27,000
-You may pass.
-Seriously?

132
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:31,000
Looks like the trick is telling
the old lady whatever she wants to hear.

133
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:33,000
Adios!

134
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:37,000
Hang on! What kind of crap is that?
There's no way that was the right answer!

135
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:40,000
We’re just supposed to say
what we think she wants to hear?

136
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:43,000
What's up with that?

137
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:46,000
-Say something.
-[crow caws]

138
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:49,000
Ugh, okay.
I’ve had just about enough of this.

139
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:53,000
-I’m gonna find my own way!
-[old lady] It's too late for that.

140
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:58,000
Refuse to take the quiz if you wish.
But know you’ll be disqualified.

141
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:00,000
Grr, that's nuts!

142
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:03,000
Different people would answer that
in different ways!

143
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:07,000
There’s no right answer for that question
and never has been.

144
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:10,000
[gasps] There is no right answer?

145
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:12,000
-I see.
-Oh?

146
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:14,000
-Leorio!
-That's enough!

147
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:20,000
[old lady] The boy with the cat eyes
has figured it out.

148
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:23,000
I don’t want to hear another word
out of you.

149
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:26,000
Say anything but your answer
and you’re disqualified.

150
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:32,000
[Kurapika] You can do this, Leorio.
This is just a simple trick.

151
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:35,000
Gon...

152
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:37,000
And now here is your question.

153
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:39,000
-[horn tooting]
-[crow caws]

154
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:42,000
You learn both your son and your daughter
have been kidnapped.

155
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:45,000
You will only be able
to rescue one of them.

156
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:48,000
Choose one for your son,
and two for your daughter.

157
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:51,000
Which of these two will you rescue?

158
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:54,000
[Leorio] Grr! She's messing with us!

159
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:59,000
[old lady] Five... four...

160
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:01,000
[Leorio] Go ahead and count down,
you old hag.

161
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:03,000
...three...

162
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:06,000
two...

163
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:09,000
-[Leorio grunts]
-...one!

164
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:14,000
[mimics buzzer] Time is up!

165
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:19,000
[yells]

166
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:27,000
Out of the way, Kurapika!

167
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:30,000
This old hag needs to be taught a lesson
and I’m gonna make sure she gets it!

168
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:32,000
Would you please calm down?

169
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:34,000
How the hell do you expect me
to calm down?

170
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:37,000
We got it right!
Do you really want to jeopardize that?

171
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:39,000
We did?

172
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:42,000
We’ve already given the correct response

173
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:45,000
Silence. Any other answer
would have been incorrect.

174
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:48,000
[Leorio] What do you mean, "silence"?

175
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:51,000
Just that. You said it yourself, remember?

176
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:52,000
[Leorio] Huh?

177
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:55,000
There’s no right answer for that question
and never has been!

178
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:56,000
You were right.

179
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:59,000
There was no correct answer
to our question.

180
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:02,000
However, we had to say "one" or "two"
as a response.

181
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:06,000
And so, our only choice was to respond
with silence.

182
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:08,000
What about that guy? He made it through!

183
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:12,000
She never told him he was correct.
All she said was “you may pass.”

184
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:16,000
Which means that this is not the path
to the Hunter Exam.

185
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:17,000
Right?

186
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:20,000
Hmm. That is correct.

187
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:25,000
The real path is right over here.

188
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:30,000
Follow this path for two hours
and you will reach the lone cedar tree.

189
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:34,000
Okay. I was not expecting this.

190
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:37,000
There is a couple that live
in a small cabin under that tree

191
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:40,000
who will serve as Navigators
on your journey.

192
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:42,000
They will guide you to the Exam site,

193
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:45,000
if you live up to their expectations,
that is.

194
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:51,000
I’m sorry. I hope you’ll forgive me
for being rude.

195
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:53,000
Don't be. I don't mind.

196
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:58,000
Meeting people like you is the only reason
I do this job in the first place.

197
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:04,000
Do your best. Become the best Hunter
you can be.

198
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:08,000
[chuckles] Sure.

199
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:11,000
-[Gon groans]
-[Leorio] Huh?

200
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:16,000
I'm stuck.
I can't figure out the right answer.

201
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:21,000
[Leorio chuckles]
You’ve really been thinking of an answer

202
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:23,000
this whole time? You can stop now.

203
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:25,000
[Gon] Huh? But why?

204
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:27,000
[Kurapika]
Because the quiz is already over.

205
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:31,000
[Gon] I know that,
but what if... you know?

206
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:34,000
Well, what if that really happens
to me someday?

207
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:37,000
If two people are in trouble
and I can only help one of them?

208
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:39,000
Then what?

209
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:43,000
It wouldn’t be right to pick one
over the other.

210
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:46,000
But like it or not,
that’s a choice I might have to make.

211
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:49,000
I just hope that I know what to do.

212
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:57,000
[old lady] The boy is right, of course.

213
00:12:57,000 --> 00:13:00,000
That is indeed the true purpose
of this test.

214
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:04,000
The abstract may come to pass
and a Hunter must be ready.

215
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:09,000
Reality can be cruel, and it often strikes
without warning.

216
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:13,000
One must always be prepared
for these crossroads in life.

217
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:21,000
HUNTER GLOSSARY

218
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:26,000
KURAPIKA

219
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:28,000
[Leorio] Man, I can’t see a thing

220
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:31,000
“You’ll reach the top in two hours,”
she said.

221
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:34,000
Well, it was two hours, two hours ago!
[tuts]

222
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:40,000
Another “Beware of Magical Beasts” sign?

223
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:44,000
I’m starting to think we’re never gonna
find this stupid Exam site.

224
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:47,000
Guys, I'm so hungry!
I need to take a dump!

225
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:50,000
-[Gon] Try to keep up, Leorio!
-I need to pee too! Hey, guys?

226
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:52,000
-I think I see it.
-[Gon] Huh?

227
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:58,000
[knocking on door]

228
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:00,000
[Leorio] Hey? Anybody home?

229
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:02,000
I guess not.

230
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:06,000
[Leorio] Coming in!

231
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:10,000
[all] Huh?

232
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:13,000
[beast cackling]

233
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:15,000
-[Leorio] Magical Beast.
-[Gon] A what?

234
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:19,000
It appears to be a Kiriko.
It can take on human form!

235
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:21,000
-They’re extremely intelligent.
-[woman whimpering]

236
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:23,000
He’s got a woman.

237
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:25,000
And the guy on the floor looks
like he needs a doctor, bad!

238
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:34,000
Please help. Save her!
You have to save my wife.

239
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:36,000
Leorio, see to his injuries!

240
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:37,000
Right! I'm on it!

241
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:49,000
[Kurapika] Even in pitch darkness,
he can still see and keep pace

242
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:51,000
with such a faint shadow.

243
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:54,000
[Gon grunting]

244
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:56,000
Impressive.

245
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:02,000
[Gon] Kiriko, let the lady go!

246
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:04,000
Why don’t you try to take her from me?

247
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:06,000
[yelps]

248
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:10,000
You hear that? It can talk.
That’s amazing!

249
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:14,000
The Kiriko is a Magical Beast
capable of human speech.

250
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:17,000
Really? Well, that ought to make this
a lot easier.

251
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,000
-Hey, come here, you dumb Kiriko!
-What?

252
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:26,000
[Kiriko] This kid's fast.

253
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:29,000
Kurapika!

254
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:36,000
[pants] Damn, that was reckless.

255
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:39,000
Stupid kid! You're gonna pay!

256
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:40,000
Hey, wait up!

257
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:49,000
Are you hurt, miss?
Are you feeling pain anywhere at all?

258
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:53,000
I'm fine, but... what about my husband?
Is he alright?

259
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:56,000
Not to worry.
Our friend is taking good care of him.

260
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:59,000
Then please. You have to take me to him,
I beg you!

261
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:02,000
[Leorio] Huh? Those tattoos...

262
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:08,000
-Wait, you're not--
-[Leorio] Kurapika.

263
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:10,000
-Huh?
-You okay?

264
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:11,000
Leorio.

265
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:14,000
[Leorio] Guess you are. What a relief.

266
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:16,000
How is the man you were caring for?

267
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:18,000
Good! I think he’ll pull through fine.

268
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:21,000
Lucky for him, the wound wasn’t
as deep as it looked,

269
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:25,000
I gave him some painkillers
so he’s sleeping it off back at the cabin

270
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:26,000
I see.

271
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:29,000
[grunts]

272
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:37,000
[snickers] How'd you know?

273
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:42,000
How could you tell that I was an imposter?

274
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:48,000
[Kurapika] To be honest,
I didn’t actually think you were.

275
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:52,000
You see, Leorio made a promise
that he’d take care of that injured man.

276
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:57,000
When I saw him,
I assumed he had left the man all alone.

277
00:16:58,000 --> 00:16:59,000
And with the Magical Beast
still on the loose,

278
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:02,000
I attacked him for abandoning
his obligation.

279
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:03,000
Nothing more.

280
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:05,000
[Kiriko snickers]

281
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:10,000
[Kurapika] And you, tell me right now.

282
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:13,000
Who are you and what is it
you want from us?

283
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:23,000
[Gon] Wait!

284
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:47,000
[Kiriko cackling]
You're pretty fast for a kid, you know?

285
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:50,000
You really hit me.
I didn't expect that from you.

286
00:17:56,000 --> 00:18:00,000
That's quite an accomplishment.
Unfortunately for you,

287
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:03,000
it comes with a higher price
than you bargained for.

288
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:07,000
Kiri, kiri, kiri, kiri, kiri!

289
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:14,000
-So, who are you?
-[Kiriko grunts]

290
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:21,000
You're not the one I was chasing, are you?
The one that I hit?

291
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:23,000
Um... are you a friend of his?

292
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:29,000
[Kiriko] Hold on. How can you tell
that I'm not the same one from before?

293
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:32,000
Huh? Oh, well, you look totally different.

294
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:36,000
Your voice is different, too.
It's higher and kinda thinner.

295
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:42,000
[Kiriko chuckles then laughs hysterically]

296
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:45,000
What's up? Why are you laughing?
Is it something I said?

297
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:51,000
[Kiriko] Hey! Hey, honey! Come here!
You’re gonna get a kick out of this!

298
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:56,000
[Kiriko 1 chuckles] How many years
has it been

299
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:58,000
since anyone was able
to tell the two of us apart?

300
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:00,000
[Kiriko 2] I'm so happy.

301
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:03,000
Can you tell ‘em apart? Seriously.

302
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:05,000
No, not at all.

303
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:09,000
Don’t you see? The Kiriko that Kurapika
and I hit is actually the husband.

304
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:12,000
[Leorio and Kurapika]
And which one is that, exactly?

305
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:14,000
[Kiriko 1]
Allow us to introduce ourselves.

306
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:16,000
We are the Navigators.

307
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:19,000
Our family provides support
for the Hunter Exam.

308
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:22,000
-I'm their daughter.
-I'm their son.

309
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:25,000
[Leorio]
Man. Great job. You sure had us fooled

310
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:28,000
The Exam site moves around.
Keeps it interesting.

311
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:32,000
But that’s exactly why they relocate it
every year. Understand?

312
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:35,000
They hire Navigators like us to help
by guiding worthy applicants

313
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:36,000
to the examination site.

314
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:39,000
Oh, so that how it works?

315
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:43,000
But don’t get the wrong idea.
We don’t help every candidate.

316
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:47,000
[son] First, we test them to see if
they’re even qualified to take the Exam.

317
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:49,000
Make sure they have what it takes.

318
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:52,000
-[daughter] Mr. Kurapika?
-Yes?

319
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:55,000
We made certain that we only gave you
the most vague of hints

320
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:57,000
but you were still able to pick up on them

321
00:19:57,000 --> 00:20:00,000
and determine that we weren’t
actually a married couple.

322
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:02,000
You only caught a glimpse of my tattoos.

323
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:05,000
But you knew that in this region,
these tattoos are only worn

324
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:08,000
by women who’ve taken a vow of chastity

325
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:12,000
Mr. Kurapika demonstrated
that he’s incredibly knowledgeable.

326
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:15,000
Therefore, he passes.

327
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:17,000
-[Kurapika sighs in relief]
-Way to go, Kurapika.

328
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:18,000
Thanks.

329
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:21,000
-[son] Mr. Leorio?
-Yes?

330
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:25,000
You, sir, unfortunately never realized
that I wasn’t who I claimed to be.

331
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:26,000
[gulps]

332
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:29,000
[son] However, you dressed my wounds
faster and more thoroughly

333
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:31,000
than any doctor.
More importantly,

334
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:34,000
you demonstrated admirable empathy
and kindness

335
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:38,000
by continuing to reassure me
that my wife would be okay.

336
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:41,000
-[Gon and Kurapika chuckling]
-Knock it off, okay? It's embarrassing.

337
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:45,000
[son] It’s clear to me
that your compassion makes you worthy

338
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:46,000
of taking the Hunter Exam.

339
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:49,000
And so, you pass.

340
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:54,000
Wait, seriously? [sighs in relief]

341
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:55,000
You did it!

342
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:57,000
[both chuckle]

343
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:01,000
-[Kurapika 1] And finally, Mr. Gon.
-Yes?

344
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:06,000
Your superhuman physical ability
and your powers of observation defy logic.

345
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:10,000
You, too, are worthy
to take the Hunter Exam.

346
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:12,000
So, you pass.

347
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:13,000
[gasps]

348
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:18,000
[chuckles]

349
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:24,000
[Kurapika 1] Alright! We’ll now take you
straight to the site of the Exam!

350
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:28,000
Oh, wow! Isn’t it incredible
that we all passed?

351
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:31,000
[Kurapika] I wouldn't celebrate just yet.

352
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:33,000
We’ve merely earned the right
to take the Exam.

353
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:37,000
[Leorio] It's progress!
I say that calls for a little celebration!

354
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:39,000
[Kurapika] Honestly, have some foresight.

355
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:42,000
Do you have to be such a smartass
all the time-- [yells]

356
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:46,000
[Kurapika 2] Hey, stop squirming!
If you fall, it's your own fault.

357
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:48,000
[laughing]

358
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:52,000
[narrator] And so, Gon and his friends
enjoy a brief journey through the sky.

359
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:58,000
However, even after all this,
they have yet to reach the starting line.

360
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:02,000
[theme song playing]

361
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:31,000
[Gon] Next time! "Rivals in Survival."
I'm gonna do my best!
